  fireCompletedText: The nest is ash. Sorrel is not pleased
  smokeDescription: The player set off a smokebomb at the base of the tree. The wasps
    grew drowsy and moved along unharmed, and the path to my herb garden is clear.
    I am grateful and relieved.
  fireWithoutAskingDescription: The player burned the wasp nest with a torch without
    ever speaking to me about it. The wasps are dead. The path is clear, but they
    did not even ask before destroying them.
  fireDescription: The player burned the wasp nest with a torch after I asked them
    not to. The wasps are dead. The path is clear, but it hurts that they were destroyed
    instead of moved along.
  fireEvidenceKey: 
  villagerSmokeDescription: The wasp nest in the orchard has been cleared. The player
    smoked the wasps out for Sorrel the druid, and they no longer threaten the village.
  villagerFireDescription: The wasp nest in the orchard has been cleared. The player
    burned it with a torch, and the wasps no longer threaten the village.
  smokeReactionIntent: React out loud, in character, to the player having just smoked
    the wasps out of the nest so they moved along unharmed.
  fireReactionIntent: React out loud, in character, to the player having just burned
    the wasp nest and killed the wasps.
